{
  "_help": "How the world reacts to what a query did. when: table (or * for any), change (dropped, emptied, created, rows_added, rows_removed, rows_changed, columns_changed, became_view, a need's change such as foe_row_removed, or a statement verb such as insert, update, delete, alter; for whole casts: committed, transaction_left_open, rollback_no_transaction, commit_no_transaction, rewind), actor (player, foe or any), and optionally like_core (a created table whose name looks like a core table). speaker: foe, grimoire or ada. line_key: a key of data/i18n/<locale>.json. effect: none, foe_rages (the foe's spells hit harder until the world is rewound), foe_forgets (the foe stares at an empty book), fight_ends_confused (no winner, at the end of the round, unless rewound), refuse (the query is undone and refused with the line), forget_chart (every element hits normally), codex_unlock (unlocks the page named in page). cooldown: turns before the same reaction can fire again (99: once per fight).",
  "reactions": [
    {"id": "delete_witch_row", "when": {"table": "witch", "change": "witch_row_removed", "actor": "player"}, "speaker": "grimoire", "line_key": "reaction.delete_witch_row", "effect": "refuse", "cooldown": 0},
    {"id": "drop_witch", "when": {"table": "witch", "change": "dropped", "actor": "player"}, "speaker": "grimoire", "line_key": "reaction.drop_witch", "effect": "refuse", "cooldown": 0},
